WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:12.406
Vinnie looked so worried that Helene ran over to him.

2
00:00:12.407 --> 00:00:15.758
"What's wrong?" she said.

3
00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:17.694
Vinnie explained.

4
00:00:17.695 --> 00:00:22.411
"I have to keep the soup away from the king," he cried.

5
00:00:22.412 --> 00:00:25.474
"I'll help," said Helene.

6
00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:29.729
They followed the servant carrying the tray of soup.

7
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:34.494
In the palace, Mandy was still searching for Helene.

8
00:00:34.495 --> 00:00:37.605
She walked down another hallway.

9
00:00:37.606 --> 00:00:40.942
She heard noises.

10
00:00:40.943 --> 00:00:44.480
Quietly she opened the nearest door.

11
00:00:44.481 --> 00:00:47.688
The room was full of billiard tables.

12
00:00:47.689 --> 00:00:51.094
Men, including King Louis, were playing.

13
00:00:51.095 --> 00:00:55.010
"Oh, Your Majesty," one man laughed.

14
00:00:55.011 --> 00:00:56.759
"You win again!

15
00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.871
You are truly the champion of this game."

16
00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:02.068
King Louis smiled.

17
00:01:02.069 --> 00:01:05.277
Then he walked into the next room.

18
00:01:05.278 --> 00:01:08.875
Mandy followed, keeping out of sight.

19
00:01:08.876 --> 00:01:12.351
It was a dining room with a long table.

20
00:01:12.352 --> 00:01:15.600
Waiting servants held trays of food.

21
00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.644
"Bring me my soup!"

22
00:01:17.645 --> 00:01:20.406
said the king as he sat down.

23
00:01:20.407 --> 00:01:24.881
Mandy saw her brother and Helene right behind the servants.

24
00:01:24.882 --> 00:01:27.010
They looked scared.

25
00:01:27.011 --> 00:01:30.611
Mandy waved, but they didn't see her.

26
00:01:30.612 --> 00:01:38.486
"Ah, my favorite soup!" the king said.

27
00:01:38.487 --> 00:01:41.800
At that moment, Vinnie jumped out.

28
00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.680
"Don't eat that!" he yelled.

29
00:01:44.681 --> 00:01:49.758
Startled, the servant dropped the soup into the king's lap.

30
00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:51.750
"You idiot!"

31
00:01:51.751 --> 00:01:54.540
King Louis leaped from his seat.

32
00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:58.747
"Your Majesty, are you all right?" cried the servant.

33
00:01:58.748 --> 00:02:01.076
Everyone ran to the king.

34
00:02:01.077 --> 00:02:04.407
They tried to wipe off the spilled soup.

35
00:02:04.408 --> 00:02:09.080
"Vinnie! Helene!" Mandy shouted loudly.

36
00:02:09.081 --> 00:02:11.226
They ran to her.

37
00:02:11.227 --> 00:02:14.871
"We'd better get away!" Helene cried.

38
00:02:14.872 --> 00:02:19.206
"Oh, look at the royal clothing," said someone.

39
00:02:19.207 --> 00:02:22.957
"His coat is ruined," said another.

40
00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:26.942
"And his best hat," a servant whispered.

41
00:02:26.943 --> 00:02:28.875
"What a mess!"

42
00:02:28.876 --> 00:02:31.537
The king looked up and screamed:

43
00:02:31.538 --> 00:02:34.002
"That boy! Stop him!"

44
00:02:34.003 --> 00:02:36.363
Everyone looked around.

45
00:02:36.364 --> 00:02:40.048
In the confusion, the children had escaped.

46
00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:43.423
The children ran down a long hallway.

47
00:02:43.424 --> 00:02:46.522
"Over here!" cried Helene.

48
00:02:46.523 --> 00:02:50.003
They stopped to catch their breath in a corner.

49
00:02:50.004 --> 00:02:52.666
The guards were far behind.

50
00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:55.214
Vinnie pulled out the photo.

51
00:02:55.215 --> 00:02:59.935
"We have to get to a fountain with golden frogs," he said.

52
00:02:59.936 --> 00:03:04.335
"You must mean the Fountain of Latona," said Helene.

53
00:03:04.336 --> 00:03:06.445
"It has many frogs on it.

54
00:03:06.446 --> 00:03:09.629
It's behind the palace. I'll show you."

55
00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:13.751
The children followed her.

56
00:03:13.752 --> 00:03:16.334
Along the way Mandy asked:

57
00:03:16.335 --> 00:03:18.838
"Why did you stop King Louis?"

58
00:03:18.839 --> 00:03:20.959
Vinnie explained.

59
00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.470
"Would the king really kill someone because of his soup?" asked Mandy.

60
00:03:26.471 --> 00:03:31.334
"Only if it was truly poisoned!" laughed Helene.

61
00:03:31.335 --> 00:03:37.494
"Look, Mandy! The frogs in the picture are glowing blue!" Vinnie shouted.

62
00:03:37.495 --> 00:03:40.272
"What?" asked Helene.

63
00:03:40.273 --> 00:03:44.468
"Nothing," said Mandy.

64
00:03:44.469 --> 00:03:46.005
"There it is!"

65
00:03:46.006 --> 00:03:49.479
Helene pointed ahead.

66
00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.075
"The fountain was inspired by an ancient Greek goddess.

67
00:03:53.076 --> 00:03:56.690
She turned people into frogs if they insulted her."

68
00:03:56.691 --> 00:04:01.274
"Wow, sounds cruel," gulped Vinnie.

69
00:04:01.275 --> 00:04:03.073
Helene giggled.

70
00:04:03.074 --> 00:04:08.708
"Some people think King Louis built it to send his people a message:

71
00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:11.070
obey your king!

72
00:04:11.071 --> 00:04:13.340
Anyway, I have to get back to work.

73
00:04:13.341 --> 00:04:14.781
See you later?"

74
00:04:14.782 --> 00:04:17.352
Mandy gave her a hug.

75
00:04:17.353 --> 00:04:22.213
"Well . . . good-bye," she said, then paused.

76
00:04:22.214 --> 00:04:24.799
"I am so glad I met you!"

77
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.561
Helene looked confused.

78
00:04:27.562 --> 00:04:32.221
When Vinnie and Mandy got to the fountain, they looked back.

79
00:04:32.222 --> 00:04:36.198
Helene was walking up the steps waving.

80
00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:41.641
The grand Palace of Versailles was as beautiful as ever.

81
00:04:41.642 --> 00:04:45.034
"The frogs are glowing red," said Vinnie.

82
00:04:45.035 --> 00:04:53.463
"We're going home."
